+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  MAILER General Commands:                                          |
|                                                                    |
|  CHECK - Check if another user has mail (not yet implemented).     |
|                                                                    |
|  FORWARD - Deliver mail to a userid other than the one specified   |
|            in the headers.  It is legal to forward mail to more    |
|            than 1 address.  If you want to continue to receive     |
|            a copy of the mail at your userid, add a forward with   |
|            an address of '<*>'.                                    |
|                                                                    |
|      FORWARD ADD    destaddr                                       |
|              DELETE destaddr | ALL                                 |
|              LIST                                                  |
|                                                                    |
|  HELP | ? - Get list of commands.                                  |
|                                                                    |
|  SHOW <show-options>  - Display assorted counters, etc.            |
|                                                                    |
|  show-options:                                                     |
|                                                                    |
|    STATUS                                                          |
|     Various Mailer status variables are returned.  These are:      |
|     Since: <date time> - time of last Mailer restart.              |
|     Msgs in/out: Number of messages (mail) received and sent.      |
|     Max Multi:  Maximum number of recipients for a single message. |
|     Stack Max:  Percentage Mailer internal storage utilization.    |
|                                                                    |
|    DOMAINS <domain-name>                                           |
|     Statistics on outgoing files to other domain Mailers.          |
|                                                                    |
|    INCOMING <nodename> <userid>                                    |
|     Statistics on files received from other network Mailers.       |
|                                                                    |
|    OUTGOING <hostname>                                             |
|     Statistics on outgoing files to other network Mailers.         |
|                                                                    |
|    SPECIAL <userid>                                                |
|     Statistics on mail to special userids (i.e. SYSTEM).           |
|                                                                    |
|  SMSG - Used as a prefix to other commands causes the reply to     |
|  be sent as a machine-readable SMSG.                               |
|                                                                    |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
